 "text": "Hey, how are you? That' a common issue. Look at the face from the side, and try draw the eyes in a series of small steps. Go only as far as making two circles. You can always fill in the middle later. Another half half method is the zent exercise. Start with a line from the middle of the eye to the top of the nose. Then connect those points with a smooth curve. You' notice a difference in no time. Lots of drawing exercises help, too. Faces are best done from life or a photo, not from memory.",
